  "$comment": "This tracks the category 7/8 roster. producerFixture points at the existing production parser/adapter test which must emit the normalized event; this file never treats its own sample event as proof. HTTP success plus no emitted evidence stays unconfirmed. expected=no_execution_fact is the three-client decision for owner=generation: every generation recipe binds an evidence definition whose signals are empty (official APIs never echo back that a temperature took effect), so a generation fact could only ever sit at unconfirmed forever. Such a state bit carries zero information and reads as 'it never succeeded', so generation stays out of the execution-fact/result state machine entirely on Web, iOS and Android. This closes only the after-the-fact badge: generation recipes still authorize the legacy template, custom-fragment path/transport validation and the user's typed generation parameters on the wire.",
